    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1271" root="امن" body-key="A">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُمَّانٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَمينٌ</span>, in two places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also One
<i>who does not write;</i> as though he were (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَأَنَّهُ</span> [in
the CK <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لاَنَّهُ</span> because he is]) an <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُمِّى</span>. (K, TA.)
[But this belongs to art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ام</span>; being of the measure
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُعْلَانٌ</span>, like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُرْيَانٌ</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>A sower,</i> or <i>cultivator of land;</i> [perhaps meaning <i>a clown,</i> or
<i>boor;</i>] syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَرَّاعٌ</span>: (CK:) or <i>sowers,</i> or <i>cultivators
of land;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زُرَّاعٌ</span>: (K, TA:) in one copy of the
K <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زِرَاع</span>. (TA.)

